WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.800
GROUPING SETS gives you direct control over which
summary levels appear in

00:00:03.825 --> 00:00:08.850
the result In this query we request three grouping
sets category alone

00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:14.000
product alone and the empty grouping set The empty
parentheses represent the

00:00:14.012 --> 00:00:19.225
grand total Notice what is not requested We do not
ask for

00:00:19.250 --> 00:00:24.175
category-and-product detail in this example so
PostgreSQL does not return that level

00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:28.375
This is what makes GROUPING SETS flexible you list
only the grains

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:32.737
that the report needs The CASE expressions again use
GROUPING to label

00:00:32.763 --> 00:00:38.388
rolled-up columns The result therefore contains
category totals product totals and one

00:00:38.412 --> 00:00:42.825
overall total Run the query and identify the grain
of each row

00:00:43.712 --> 00:00:48.588
Some rows mean one category across all products Some
mean one product

00:00:48.612 --> 00:00:54.150
across all categories The final row means all data
GROUPING SETS

00:00:54.162 --> 00:00:57.038
is often a good option when a report has a specific
layout

00:00:57.062 --> 00:01:01.438
that does not fit a simple hierarchy It can replace
multiple GROUP

00:01:01.462 --> 00:01:05.650
BY queries that would otherwise need to be combined
The key skill

00:01:05.662 --> 00:01:10.338
is still grain awareness One result set can now
contain several grains

00:01:10.588 --> 00:01:13.575
so labeling and interpretation become even more
important
